# Fixture for native_codegen.feature: the subtlest case this plan's
# own third increment handles -- a local that IS the value being
# returned at ONE terminal, but is correctly discarded (decremented) at
# a DIFFERENT terminal within the SAME function. bm_nc_insert_string_
# rc_decs (native_codegen.patlang) checks this per-terminal (is THIS
# specific terminal's own preceding instruction a Load of THIS specific
# candidate name), not once globally -- a local can dominate every
# terminal yet only actually be returned at one of them.
#
# mixed_exit returns s itself when cond > 0 (ownership transfers to the
# caller for that path -- correctly NOT decremented there), but returns
# n (stringified) otherwise (s is genuinely discarded on that path --
# correctly IS decremented there). Printing the actual returned STRING
# content each cycle, compared byte-for-byte against pat --ir-run on
# the identical source (this feature's own established cross-check,
# used throughout this suite), is what actually proves correctness here
# -- a reused-too-early block corrupting the returned string's own
# content would show up as wrong output, not necessarily a crash, well
# before 50 iterations.

make a function called mixed_exit takes n, cond returns r
  let s = chr(n)
  if cond > 0 then
    return s
  end
  return n
end

let i = 0
while i < 50 do
  let r = mixed_exit(65 + (i % 10), i % 2)
  print(r)
  let i = i + 1
end
